{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/3069","id":3257070824,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz887CIvTo","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3069","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3069.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3069.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3069","number":3069,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Set node key expiration in the far future","user":{"login":"sbatista-uc","id":180049281,"node_id":"U_kgDOCrtVgQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180049281?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbatista-uc","html_url":"https://github.com/sbatista-uc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbatista-uc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbatista-uc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbatista-uc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbatista-uc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbatista-uc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbatista-uc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbatista-uc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbatista-uc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbatista-uc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I noticed that when I connected a Tailscale client using a preauthorized key it would start burning quite a few CPU cycles on the client device. Turns out the Tailscale client was spinlocking due to a bug where it sees an expiration of 0 and considers that it \"must refresh immediately\" triggering expensive key loads and checks in an infinite loop.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if this is the correct fix for the issue, would love to get some visibility from the Tailscale team to help determine what is the correct way to ensure the client knows a node's key has no expiration date.\r\n\r\nAccording to the official documentation tagged devices should have no expiry, so this is still wrong, but at least it doesn't spinlock clients: https://tailscale.com/docs/features/tags#key-expiry\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nHeadscale is \"Open Source, acknowledged contribution\", this means that any\r\ncontribution will have to be discussed with the Maintainers before being submitted.\r\n\r\nThis model has been chosen to reduce the risk of burnout by limiting the\r\nmaintenance overhead of reviewing and validating third-party code.\r\n\r\nHeadscale is open to code contributions for bug fixes without discussion.\r\n\r\nIf you find mistakes in the documentation, please submit a fix to the documentation.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n<!-- Please tick if the following things apply. You… -->\r\n\r\n- [x] have read the [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md) file\r\n- [ ] raised a GitHub issue or discussed it on the projects chat beforehand\r\n- [ ] added unit tests\r\n- [ ] added integration tests\r\n- [ ] updated documentation if needed\r\n- [ ] updated CHANGELOG.md\r\n\r\n<!-- If applicable, please reference the issue using `Fixes #XXX` and add tests to cover your new code. -->\r\n","created_at":"2026-02-07T05:41:00Z","updated_at":"2026-04-17T08:04:02Z","closed_at":"2026-04-17T08:04:02Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organi